+---
+description: Generate, review, and apply a Drizzle migration (schema ⇄ core types in sync)
+---
+
+Drive a schema change through Drizzle safely. `$ARGUMENTS` describes the change
+(e.g. "add `notes` text to set_logs", "new table program_templates"). The hard
+rule this command enforces: **`packages/db/src/schema.ts` mirrors the `@rackd/core`
+types** — change both, or the layers drift.
+
+Context (precomputed):
+
+- Schema: `packages/db/src/schema.ts`
+- Core types: `packages/core/src/types.ts`
+- Existing migrations: !`ls packages/db/drizzle 2>/dev/null | tail -5 || echo "(none yet / dir name may differ — check drizzle.config)"`
+- Pending working changes: !`git --no-pager diff --stat -- packages/db packages/core`
+
+Steps:
+
+1. **Edit the types first** (`@rackd/core` `types.ts`) — the domain shape is the source of
+   truth. Then mirror the column(s)/table in `packages/db/src/schema.ts`: same field names,
+   nullability, and units (weight columns store canonical **kg**, never lb).
+2. **Generate the migration SQL** (writes a file, does NOT touch the DB):
+   ```bash
+   pnpm --filter @rackd/db db:generate
+   ```
+3. **Review the generated SQL before applying.** Show the new file's diff. Check for:
+   - destructive ops (DROP COLUMN / TABLE, NOT NULL on an existing populated table without a
+     default, type narrowing) — call these out explicitly, they can lose data;
+   - FK actions (ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL) matching the prescription-vs-session and
+     ownership intent;
+   - the migration only contains _this_ change, nothing dragged in from local DB drift.
+4. **Apply to Postgres** (needs `DATABASE_URL`; local Supabase or the target):
+   ```bash
+   pnpm --filter @rackd/db db:push
+   ```
+   If `DATABASE_URL` isn't set / no DB is reachable, stop after step 3 and report the SQL +
+   the exact command to run when a DB is up — don't guess.
+5. **Update repo functions / routes** that read or write the new field (`packages/db/src/index.ts`),
+   and any client `qk` reads. New owned columns still scope by `ownerId`.
+6. Gate: `pnpm typecheck && pnpm test`. If repo behavior changed, run the db suite
+   (`pnpm --filter @rackd/db test`, needs Postgres) and consider the **test-author** agent for
+   cascade/scoping coverage.
+
+Report: types + schema edits, the generated SQL file, whether it was pushed (or why not),
+and any destructive op you flagged.
