index 0000000..5f19d83
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.cursor/rules/db.mdc
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+---
+description: Drizzle schema + repository function conventions for packages/db
+globs: packages/db/**/*.ts
+alwaysApply: false
+---
+
+# packages/db conventions
+
+`packages/db` is the **only place that touches Postgres** (single `pg` pool in
+`db.ts`). It owns the Drizzle schema and the repository functions; the UI never
+imports it as a value (it calls API routes that call these functions).
+
+## Repository functions
+- Functions like `startSession`, `logSet`, `finishSession` use the shared Drizzle `db` (no client argument) and are called from **API route handlers only**.
+- Signatures take `{ ownerId, … }`; **every read/write filters/sets by `ownerId`.** When mutating an existing owned row, scope the `where` by both `id` AND `ownerId` so one owner can't touch another's row.
+- Match the style of `createRoutine` / `renameRoutine`: small, single-purpose, returns the row. Keep mutations here, not in routes.
+
+## Schema ⇄ core types
+- `src/schema.ts` **mirrors the `@rackd/core` types** — same field names, nullability, units. Change the core type first, then the schema, or the layers drift.
+- Weight columns store canonical **kg**, never lb.
+- **Prescription vs session are separate trees.** `routines/routineExercises/routineSets` = the plan; `sessions/sessionExercises/setLogs` = what happened. Starting a workout deep-copies the plan into a session; logs land on the session tree. Never mutate routines to record performed sets.
+- Exercise media is **URL-only** (`thumbnailUrl`/`clipUrl`) — never store binaries.
+
+## Migrations
+- `pnpm --filter @rackd/db db:generate` writes SQL; review it before applying (watch for DROP COLUMN/TABLE, NOT NULL on populated tables, type narrowing, FK ON DELETE actions matching prescription/session + ownership intent). Then `pnpm --filter @rackd/db db:push` applies to Postgres via `DATABASE_URL`. See `/db-migrate`.
+- The exercise library is seeded once server-side with `pnpm --filter @rackd/db seed` (`src/seed-pg.ts`), not per login.
+
+## Tests
+- Repo tests run against a **real Postgres** (local Supabase / CI), truncate-per-test. Use `test/setup.ts` (truncates + re-seeds `SEED_EX`: `ex_bench`, `ex_squat`, `ex_row`) and `test/factories.ts` (`makeRoutine`, `OWNER_A`/`OWNER_B`) — never hand-roll fixtures.
+- Cover what a mock can't: ownership scoping (owner B blocked from owner A's rows), FK cascade / SET NULL on delete, prescription→session deep-copy not mutating the routine.
+- `packages/db`'s `test` script is `vitest run`; `pnpm test` (turbo) picks it up.
+
+See `@AGENTS.md` for global rules and commands.
diff --git a/.cursor/rules/web.mdc b/.cursor/rules/web.mdc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..068f61b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.cursor/rules/web.mdc
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+---
+description: Frontend + API-route conventions for the Next.js PWA (apps/web)
+globs: apps/web/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}
+alwaysApply: false
+---
+
+# apps/web conventions
+
+`apps/web` is a Next.js 15 / React 19 App Router PWA. It is a thin shell over
+`@rackd/core` (logic + types) and `@rackd/db` (data). Two layers live here: the
+client UI and the API route handlers that are the data-access layer.
+
+## Structure
+- **Feature-folder structure** (`features/<name>/` colocates components + hooks + queries), not by file-type.
+- Workspace packages ship TS source (listed in `transpilePackages`); import `@rackd/core` / `@rackd/db` directly.
+
+## Data layer (client → API → DB)
+- The **UI never touches the DB.** It calls `api()` (`lib/api.ts`) wrapped in **React Query** (`lib/query.ts`), never `@rackd/db` repo functions directly.
+- All query keys go in the central `qk` registry in `lib/query.ts`. Reads use `useQuery`; writes call `api`/`apiMutate` then `invalidateQueries`.
+- `apiMutate` queues fire-and-forget writes in IndexedDB so they survive offline (flushed FIFO on reconnect); plain `api` when the caller must see the error.
+- **Never value-import `@rackd/db` into a client component** — it pulls in `pg` and breaks the bundle. Use `import type` only.
+- Weight on the wire is canonical **kg**; convert at the display edge with `fromKg`/`formatWeight`. Never store/display raw lb.
+
+## API route handlers (`src/app/api/**`)
+- Route handlers call `@rackd/db` repository functions — they are the only place the client's requests reach Postgres.
+- **Always** wrap owner-scoped routes with `withUser` (`lib/api-auth.ts`) and derive `ownerId` from the JWT `sub`. NEVER read an `ownerId` from the body, query string, or params.
+- POST returns `201`; dynamic `[id]` params come from `await ctx.params`. Set `export const runtime = "nodejs"`.
+- The exercise + sharedRoutines libraries are the public exceptions (world-readable, owner-writable).
+
+## UI (Preline)
+- UI uses **Preline** (preferred over native controls). Preline 4 exposes `window.HSStaticMethods` only (no `window.HSSelect`); enhance via `HSStaticMethods.autoInit()`.
+- `globals.css` imports `variants.css` + `@source` by **relative path** (`../../node_modules/preline/...`) because they aren't in Preline's package `exports`.
+- `PrelineInit` re-inits on route change; wrap stateful widgets (see `AdvancedSelect`) and forward the native `change` to React.
+- Inline-styles → Preline/Tailwind migration is in progress (Stats select done first).
+
+## Gotchas
+- **Rest timer is wall-clock.** `@rackd/core`'s `timer.ts` stores an absolute `endAt`; PWA tabs sleep, so always recompute `remainingMs(state, now)`. The platform layer schedules the service-worker notification for `endAt`.
+- **Exercise media is URL-only** (`thumbnailUrl`/`clipUrl` CDN links, cached-on-view by the SW). Logging must never block on media; fall back to thumbnail + text offline.
+- `getCurrentUserId()` (`lib/auth.ts`) resolves the Supabase user id for client-side reads/keys only — never hardcode an `ownerId`.
+
+See `@AGENTS.md` for global rules and commands.
